    "maskRule": "real buildings whose centroid falls inside a mask (plus a 24 m skirt) are not drawn; real terrain inside the skirt is blended toward the authored ground",
    "coastlineTransition": "The authored harbour basin south of the district (Z 45..140) opens east through an authored channel, about Z 90..140 from X 168 to X ~450, into the real inner harbour where the NOAA Bridgeport gauge stands (city X 530.4, Z 223.1). Real chunks yield to the channel; its banks are authored quays that step down to real DEM terrain over the 24 m skirt. Water everywhere is one plane at the snapshot water level.",
    "verticalProposal": {
      "cityYFromNavd88": "cityY = navd88M - 0.23",
      "reason": "puts Bridgeport mean sea level (-0.067 m NAVD88, 1983-2001 epoch) on the authored water top (-0.3 m); real streets then sit ~3-5 m above the authored quay and meet it on the skirt ramp"
    },
    "realCropsRelation": {
      "bridgeport-harbor-west": "south of the authored mask (city Z 370..927); the strip Z 140..370 is real geography to fill from the statewide overview"
    }
  },
